{"metadata":{"description":"Loom Chat is a DSH Web client plugin that turns linear ordinary sessions into a pannable, zoomable Loom-style canvas for parallel exploration.","id":"gh:1351226463","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-plugin-loom-chat","slug":"onenameneo/dsh-plugin-loom-chat","topics":["chat-ui","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Loom Chat is a DSH Web client plugin that turns linear ordinary sessions into a pannable, zoomable L"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"oom-style canvas for parallel exploration."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-loom-chat"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Loom Chat is a DSH Web client plugin that turns linear ordinary sessions into a pannable, zoomable L"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"oom-style canvas for parallel exploration."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文说明 · GitHub repository"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Loom project"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Loom is a local Agent workbench that turns AI conversations into an explorable space for thinking. I"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"t combines streamed conversations with a branching canvas, project-based files and sessions, deliber"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ate context management, Agent tools, MCP servers, long-term memory, and local Agent activity trackin"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"g. A question can be split into multiple lines of investigation, arranged as a thought graph, and co"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"ntinued with the right context on each branch. Loom is designed for research, learning, writing, cod"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"ing, and other work that benefits from sustained thinking and parallel exploration. This plugin brin"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"gs Loom's branching-canvas experience to DSH Web as a lightweight companion."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Loom Chat is available as an npm package with prebuilt browser code. Install it without a tag to rec"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"eive the current `latest` release:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Latest release"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Install from GitHub"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Use the repository source when you need the latest unreleased commit:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"GitHub installs build the package locally through its `prepare` script. If pnpm asks for permission "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"to run the build, add the exact package name it reports to the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml` under"},{"id":"p14s3","text":" `allowBuilds`, then run the install command again. Prefer the npm installation for normal use becau"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"se it downloads prebuilt artifacts."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"To update or remove the plugin:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The plugin contributes to the `web` profile only; it does not modify the DSH native sidebar or repla"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ce the native conversation renderer."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"It is designed for exploring several directions around one question: keep the main session as the co"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ntext origin, fork new questions into independent sessions, and inspect the resulting paths together"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ork new questions into independent sessions, and inspect the resulting paths together on the canvas."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"- Every Canvas window can read its transcript, edit its draft, send a message, and stop generation i"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ndependently.
- Canvas transcript rendering is owned by this plugin: it displays text/Markdown, code"},{"id":"p20s3","text":", reasoning, tool and status summaries, commands, context, attachment references, and readable fallb"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"acks for unknown content shapes.
- A message or text selection can start a branch. The child inherit"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"s the DSH context before the fork boundary, while selected text remains as a reference card at the t"},{"id":"p20s6","text":"op of the child session.
- Child sessions are independent and can branch to unlimited depth. The plu"},{"id":"p20s7","text":"gin does not copy rendered messages or synchronize later messages automatically.
- Use native single"},{"id":"p20s8","text":"-session mode when you need the full host composer, including attachments, slash commands, model sel"},{"id":"p20s9","text":"ection, or Plan controls."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Usage demo"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Open Loom from the native DSH session header to pan and zoom across the canvas. Use the branch actio"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"n on any session window to continue exploring from that context. Every branch keeps its own history,"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" draft, and runtime state, so several lines of thought can move forward in parallel."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"_Opening the Loom canvas from a native session._"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"_Viewing related but independent conversations together on one canvas._"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Why “Loom”"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"“Loom” is a weaving machine. A conversation can be thought of as a thread of reasoning: it starts fr"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"om a main session, branches into different directions, and unfolds in parallel on the same canvas. L"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"oom Chat is named for the way it weaves those separate lines of exploration into a visible, extensib"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"le conversation network instead of flattening them into a single linear record."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Interaction model"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **Canvas mode**: the default view shows the complete tree containing the current session (parents,"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" sibling branches, and descendants). The canvas supports pan, zoom, node selection, and branching fr"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"om any window.
- **Interactive windows**: every visible session keeps its own projected transcript, "},{"id":"p28s4","text":"draft, send action, stop action, and running/error state. Multiple sessions can run side by side wit"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"hout opening one over another. Deleting a window requires confirmation and archives its descendants "},{"id":"p28s6","text":"together.
- **Single-session mode**: opening a node returns to DSH's native conversation surface, in"},{"id":"p28s7","text":"cluding the native composer, tools, attachments, Plan, model selection, and projections.
- **Mode sw"},{"id":"p28s8","text":"itching**: clicking a window only selects it; the window's Chat action enters native focus mode. The"},{"id":"p28s9","text":" native session header exposes a Loom entry action; returning to Canvas restores the selected node a"},{"id":"p28s10","text":"nd the in-memory viewport for the current page.
- **Unlimited depth**: Canvas recursively derives li"},{"id":"p28s11","text":"neage from each session's `parentId` without a branch-depth limit.
- **Navigation and performance**:"},{"id":"p28s12","text":" Entering Canvas locates the current session. The toolbar provides locate-current and reset controls"},{"id":"p28s13","text":". Subtrees can be collapsed, existing nodes keep their slots while messages, titles, or status chang"},{"id":"p28s14","text":"e, and cold histories load on demand near the viewport or selected node while offscreen sessions use"},{"id":"p28s15","text":"es load on demand near the viewport or selected node while offscreen sessions use lightweight cards."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Context inheritance"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Privacy & permissions"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Based on its current runtime code, Loom Chat:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- does not directly send data to third-party servers;
- does not read API keys or environment variab"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"les;
- does not execute shell commands;
- uses DSH's public session, runtime, conversation, workspac"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"e, and UI APIs;
- stores Loom branch presentation metadata, including derived titles and boundaries,"},{"id":"p33s4","text":" in browser `localStorage`;
- can open, fork, rename, cancel, and archive DSH sessions when requeste"},{"id":"p33s5","text":"d through the plugin UI."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"- DSH Web profile with the public session, runtime, conversation, workspace, and UI slot APIs.
- DSH"},{"id":"p35s2","text":" package line `0.1.x`, tested against the aligned `0.1.0-rc.7` public package set; the peer dependen"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"cy range is `<0.2.0`.
- The plugin follows the DSH developer-preview APIs; compatibility can change "},{"id":"p35s4","text":"as DSH evolves.
- Local development and package builds require Node.js `^22.19.0` or `>=24.0.0` and "},{"id":"p35s5","text":".
- Local development and package builds require Node.js `^22.19.0` or `>=24.0.0` and pnpm `11.7.0`."}],"truncated":true}
